,52,62,70,72,70,66,64,66,72,76,74,66,52,32],[12,8,6,4,4,6,11,19,31,44,56,66,72,72,68,64,64,70,78,84,80,68,50,28]],narrative:["Instagram has two peaks a day and they are not the same size. The lunch block, roughly 11:00 to 13:00, is a real rise and tops out around 12:00 on a weekday. The evening block is bigger: attention climbs from 17:00, passes the lunch peak by 18:00, and reaches its high point at 19:00 before falling away after 21:00.","Midweek is where those peaks are strongest. Wednesday 19:00 is the single best cell in the Instagram grid, with Tuesday and Thursday a point or two behind it, and Monday and Friday noticeably softer at the same hour. Nothing about a Friday evening post is wrong, it just starts from a lower base than the same post on Wednesday.","Weekends behave differently rather than badly. Saturday flattens out into a long plateau from midday to about 20:00, so the exact minute matters less, and Sunday evening comes back up to weekday strength at 19:00. If you only post five times a week, the weekday evenings earn the slots. If you post seven, Sunday evening is the one weekend slot worth protecting."]},facebook:{grid:[[6,4,3,3,5,10,20,34,50,62,66,64,66,70,68,62,56,52,50,48,46,40,28,14],[6,4,3,3,5,11,22,36,54,66,70,68,70,74,72,66,58,54,52,50,48,42,29,15],[7,4,3,3,5,11,22,37,55,67,71,69,71,75,73,67,59,55,53,51,49,43,30,15],[7,4,3,3,5,11,21,35,53,65,69,67,69,73,71,65,57,53,51,49,47,41,29,15],[7,5,4,3,5,10,19,32,48,60,64,62,64,66,64,58,52,48,46,44,42,38,28,16],[9,6,4,3,4,7,13,22,34,44,50,52,54,56,54,50,46,44,44,44,42,38,28,17],[9,6,4,3,4,7,14,24,37,48,54,56,58,60,58,54,50,48,50,52,50,44,32,18]],narrative:["Facebook is the daytime network in this set. It wakes up early, is already strong by 09:00, and peaks at 13:00 on every weekday. There is a second high point in the middle of the morning around 10:00 and a shoulder at 14:00, which together make 09:00 to 14:00 the block that matters.","The evening is the mirror image of Instagram. By 19:00 a weekday has fallen back to roughly two thirds of its 13:00 level and it keeps sliding until midnight. Posting a Facebook update at 20:00 because that is when you finished work is the most common avoidable mistake on this network.","Weekends are quieter across the board, with Saturday the weakest day of the seven, and the shape flattens: Sunday holds a mild bump from midday through the early evening rather than showing a clear peak. Save Saturday for something evergreen and put anything time sensitive on Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday around lunchtime."]},threads:{grid:[[10,7,5,4,5,8,15,25,36,46,54,60,66,64,58,56,58,64,72,80,84,78,60,32],[10,7,5,4,5,9,17,28,40,50,58,64,70,68,62,60,62,68,76,84,88,80,62,33],[11,7,5,4,6,9,17,28,40,50,58,64,70,68,62,60,62,68,76,85,89,81,63,34],[11,7,5,4,6,9,16,27,39,49,57,63,69,67,61,59,61,67,75,83,87,79,62,33],[11,8,6,5,6,9,15,25,36,45,53,59,64,62,57,55,57,62,70,76,78,72,58,34],[14,10,7,5,5,7,11,18,28,38,46,54,60,60,58,56,56,60,66,72,76,72,58,36],[14,10,7,5,5,7,12,20,31,41,49,56,62,62,58,56,58,64,72,80,84,76,58,32]],narrative:["Threads runs on Instagram time shifted about an hour later. The evening conversation block is the whole story: it builds from 18:00, peaks at 20:00 on every single day of the week, and is still strong at 21:00 when Instagram has already started to fade.","The late-night floor is the highest of any text network here. At 23:00 Threads is still scoring about double what X or Facebook manage at the same hour, and midnight holds low double digits where LinkedIn is barely above zero. It is not a peak, but it is not dead air either.","Weekdays beat weekends, with Tuesday and Wednesday at 20:00 the strongest cells in the grid, but the gap is small compared to LinkedIn. Sunday evening comes back to within a few points of a Monday, so a seven-day posting rhythm costs you very little here."]},linkedin:{grid:[[2,1,1,1,2,5,14,32,58,74,80,76,72,66,60,54,44,32,20,12,8,6,4,3],[2,1,1,1,3,6,17,38,68,86,92,86,80,74,66,58,48,34,21,13,9,6,4,3],[2,1,1,1,3,6,17,38,68,86,92,86,80,74,66,58,48,34,21,13,9,6,4,3],[2,1,1,1,3,6,16,36,65,82,88,83,77,71,64,56,46,33,20,12,8,6,4,3],[2,1,1,1,2,5,14,30,54,68,74,70,66,58,50,42,34,24,16,10,7,5,3,2],[1,1,1,1,1,2,4,8,14,20,24,26,26,24,22,20,18,14,10,8,6,4,3,2],[1,1,1,1,1,2,5,10,18,26,32,34,34,32,28,26,24,22,18,16,14,10,6,3]],narrative:["LinkedIn is a working-hours network and the grid shows it more sharply than anywhere else. Weekday mornings between 09:00 and 11:00 carry the platform, 10:00 is the peak on all five weekdays, and Tuesday and Wednesday at 10:00 are the two strongest cells in the whole dataset for this network.","The fall after lunch is steady rather than sudden. By 15:00 a weekday is at roughly two thirds of its 10:00 level, by 17:00 it is at about a third, and after 18:00 it collapses. An evening LinkedIn post is competing for attention that has left the building.","The weekend is the most extreme drop of any network here: a whole Saturday adds up to less than a third of a Wednesday, and its best hour barely reaches what a weekday manages before 08:00. Treat Saturday and Sunday as off, and spend the effort on getting Tuesday to Thursday mornings right instead."]},twitter:{grid:[[8,5,4,3,5,10,22,40,58,66,68,66,70,68,62,58,60,64,62,56,50,42,28,15],[8,5,4,3,5,11,24,44,64,72,74,72,76,74,68,63,65,69,66,60,53,44,29,16],[9,6,4,3,6,11,24,44,64,72,74,72,76,74,68,63,65,69,66,60,53,44,29,16],[9,6,4,3,6,11,23,42,61,69,71,69,73,71,65,60,62,66,64,58,51,43,29,16],[9,6,5,4,6,10,21,38,55,62,64,62,66,63,57,52,54,57,55,50,45,39,28,17],[11,8,6,4,5,7,13,22,34,42,46,48,50,50,48,46,46,48,48,46,44,40,30,19],[11,8,6,4,5,8,14,24,37,46,52,54,56,56,54,52,54,58,60,58,54,46,32,18]],narrative:["X is a commute and lunch network. It wakes up on the way to work: between 06:00 and 09:00 a weekday triples, then holds that level all the way through to 13:00 with the peak at 12:00.","Unlike Facebook there is a real second wind. Late afternoon, around 16:00 to 17:00, lifts back near the mor